Licensing here is **per portion**, not a dual license over every file:

- Original contributions of this project: MIT (the text above).
- Anything copied from, or derived from, `dsh-context`: Apache-2.0, with the
  upstream notices preserved (`NOTICE`, `UPSTREAM.md`).

As of the M0 documentation stage **no upstream source code has been copied into
this repository yet**, so there is currently no Apache-2.0-licensed portion
here; `LICENSE-Apache-2.0` / `NOTICE` / `UPSTREAM.md` exist so that provenance
and notices are in place before the upstream source is brought in (M1). Once
such a portion exists, the combined distribution is conventionally described as
`MIT AND Apache-2.0` in `package.json`; that string describes the combination,
not a second license on our own files.
